WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.700
Marvel Studios is apparently taking a bit
of a breather this summer, pressing pause

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:09.260
on its production schedule after wrapping
up phase 3 of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:13.599
The slowdown seems set to start after the
launches of Avengers: Endgame in April and

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.940
Spider-Man: Far From Home in July.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:20.720
Taking to Twitter in late February, Deadpool
co-creator Rob Liefeld offered an intriguing

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:25.220
observation about where he thinks the MCU
is heading beyond 2019.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.789
As the writer and artist pointed out, after
Endgame and Far From Home, it looks as though

00:00:29.789 --> 00:00:34.300
it will be about a year before another Marvel
film is rolled out into theaters.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.420
As Liefeld wrote in a Twitter post,

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.860
After Far From Home makes its debut, the next
scheduled release date for a Marvel Studios

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:55.879
film is May 1, 2020, and as of the start of
March 2019, it's not publicly known what that

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:56.960
movie is going to be.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.420
Whatever it is, that leaves roughly 10 months
between the Spider-Man sequel and Marvel's

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:02.740
mystery project.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:07.120
Prolific comic book writer Mark Millar, the
writer behind influential properties like

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:11.939
Wanted, Kick-Ass, and Kingsman: The Secret
Service, joined in on the conversation on

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.540
Twitter, replying to Liefeld's original tweet
with his own thoughts.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.060
The writer noted that this might be the first
time in over ten years that there's been this

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.740
wide of a gap between MCU releases.

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:27.939
He also argues that it's a good thing, calling
the apparent cooldown, quote, "a wise move."

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:30.460
He explained his take further by writing,

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.880
While Millar has never been too closely involved
with Marvel on the movie making side, he's

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:46.859
no stranger to working with the company's
characters, having written for such series

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:52.180
as Ultimate Fantastic Four, Ultimate X-Men,
and Marvel Knights Spider-Man, among others.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:57.500
So while he does possess some insider insight,
he seems to be as in the dark about Marvel

00:01:57.509 --> 00:01:59.829
Studios' specific plans as any other fan.

00:01:59.829 --> 00:02:05.970
In 2014, Marvel Studios released a massive
roadmap for the next few years of MCU content,

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:10.649
culminating in the two-part Infinity War and
the since-scrapped Inhumans movie.

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:14.819
Now that we're reaching the end of that sequence,
the future of the series feels more unknown

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:15.900
than ever.

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:20.190
The secrecy makes sense: it's been pointed
out that revealing the MCU's future plans

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:25.000
before Endgame's release could potentially
spoil the events of Endgame, especially if

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:28.360
that climactic movie kills off an Avenger
or two for good.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:32.650
With that in mind, the studio playing things
close to the vest is understandable, and there

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:35.489
are probably some benefits to a short hiatus
too.

00:02:35.489 --> 00:02:40.890
While superhero fatigue hasn't kicked in with
audiences yet, it remains a real possibility,

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:45.350
and Marvel could be wise to take a moment
after Endgame to enjoy a victory lap before

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:48.870
getting audiences excited for its next few
dozen movies.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:53.459
For over a decade now, the studio has been
cranking out films at a blistering pace, kicking

00:02:53.459 --> 00:02:57.939
off the MCU's first phase with six movies
in the span of four years.

00:02:57.939 --> 00:03:02.129
For phase two and beyond, the company picked
up the pace, seemingly pushing its luck by

00:03:02.129 --> 00:03:05.500
bringing out as many as three movies in one
year.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:09.829
That's what happened in 2018, when fans were
treated to Black Panther, Avengers: Infinity

00:03:09.829 --> 00:03:12.040
War, and Ant-Man and the Wasp.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:16.190
Whether the series has taken us to space,
other dimensions, unknown countries, or the

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:21.299
microscopic Quantum Realm, it's all been accelerating
toward Endgame, which has been described as

00:03:21.299 --> 00:03:26.540
a conclusion of sorts to the MCU's staggering
story arc about the all-powerful Infinity

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.300
Stones.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.140
"Thanos has been inside my head for six years."

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:34.849
That story ending should provide a natural
reason to put things on pause, maybe just

00:03:34.849 --> 00:03:38.590
to take a second and count all the money the
series has made.

00:03:38.590 --> 00:03:43.030
Considering the two billion dollar box office
performance of Avengers: Infinity War, which

00:03:43.030 --> 00:03:48.180
you may recall ended in a devastating cliffhanger,
it's all but guaranteed that the fourth Avengers

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.420
will be among the biggest releases of all
time, capping off a decade-plus of unprecedented,

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.170
runaway success.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:59.510
The Spider-Man sequel, taking the webslinger
out of America for the first time for a European

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:03.530
tour with Mysterio, also seems poised to do
big numbers.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:08.290
So 2020 looks like the perfect time for Marvel
to scale things back for a little bit, allowing

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:13.150
both creators and fans time to catch their
breath and get excited again for new stories

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.150
to come.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:18.940
While the specifics are still unknown to the
public, Marvel Studios head honcho Kevin Feige

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:23.440
has offered a few general teasers for the
upcoming fourth phase of the MCU.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:28.610
Speaking to Collider during a Captain Marvel
press junket, Feige teased the all-new, all-different

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:33.810
future of the series, telling viewers to definitely
expect more obscure comic characters to get

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:37.350
pulled off the company's deep bench for the
feature film treatment.

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:38.480
As the producer put it,

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:04.160
He continued, sharing that the film about
the Eternals is in the pipeline for the post-Endgame

00:05:04.160 --> 00:05:05.100
MCU.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:09.980
That movie, he says, will introduce a whole
new group of legendary heroes to the MCU at

00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:10.600
once.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:11.600
Feige said,

00:05:22.700 --> 00:05:27.880
He also left open the possibility for a movie
with epic scope, taking audiences far back

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.420
into the past of the MCU, saying,

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:47.580
While Marvel may be taking a short pause from
theatrical releases, we can still expect new

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.220
content.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:53.640
In an intriguing move, the studio is developing
several television series set in the MCU to

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:57.370
launch on Disney's upcoming streaming platform
Disney+.

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:02.370
Unlike the Netflix or ABC series, which are
produced by Marvel Television, these shows

00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:07.700
will be full-fledged Marvel Studios productions,
featuring movie characters and sporting big

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.360
budgets.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.100
"Reality can be whatever I want."

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:15.460
The series lineup includes a show about Tom
Hiddleston's trickster god Loki, which is

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:18.080
expected to premiere later in 2019.

00:06:18.080 --> 00:06:22.660
Also reportedly in the works are a team-up
series with Falcon and the Winter Soldier,

00:06:22.660 --> 00:06:25.960
and another project centering on Vision and
Scarlet Witch.

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:30.410
Rumor has it that there may even be a project
in the pipeline centering on Clint Barton's

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.970
Hawkeye training Kate Bishop, his eagle-eyed
successor.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:38.410
So rest easy, true believers, we're getting
more Marvel content than we know what to do

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:39.410
with.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:42.000
All it's going to take is just a little bit
of patience.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.980
There are some movies we know the company
is working on, including Eternals, Black Widow,

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:51.340
and sequels to Black Panther, Doctor Strange,
and the Guardians of the Galaxy, but when

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:54.450
these movies will officially appear is still
up in the air.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:58.610
But Feige has assured fans that the company
has a slate of movies ready to go all the

00:06:58.610 --> 00:07:00.660
way up through 2025.

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.440
Who could we be seeing in the future?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.440
Ms. Marvel?

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:04.440
The Thunderbolts?

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:08.910
Or could we soon start seeing Marvel Studios'
takes on X-Men and the Fantastic Four?

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:13.880
The possibilities feel limitless, but before
we can get to all of that, we've got business

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:15.910
to take care of with Thanos.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:20.030
It may be the end of an era, but it's also
the start of something new.

